  "body": "7.8.12 Aborting a Document doesn't say anything about whether or not to fire the load event to the Document (if it hasn't yet been fired).\r\n\r\nIt appears that Gecko will currently fire load, if we were currently blocking the load event due to pending sub-resources. WebKit/blink appear not to.\r\n\r\nThe steps also say we should abort the parser, which changes the readyState. It appears that all implementations do change the state, but only gecko is firing readystatechange.\r\n\r\nGecko also fires pageshow if it hadn't already done so.\r\n\r\nI want to change Gecko to match (not fire any events from within abort), but we should clarify the spec around this.",
